Hearse will not overwrite an existing bones file.  If it's run with the 
/delete option, each submitted bones file will be removed from your 
machine (and so, in effect, replaced with another bones file, though 
there is no guarantee that the bones file downloaded will be from the 
same level as the one deleted)

The idea, though, is to simulate a multi-user machine.  Users who invoke 
Hearse with the default options will end up with more bones files than 
they normally would have.

